1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:03,943
November 2000.

2
00:00:03,983 --> 00:00:07,112
A satellite looks down
at a patch of the Persian Gulf.

3
00:00:07,152 --> 00:00:08,784
There is no island here.

4
00:00:08,824 --> 00:00:10,103
Just sea.

5
00:00:10,705 --> 00:00:12,673
November 2003.

6
00:00:12,713 --> 00:00:14,085
The same place.

7
00:00:14,176 --> 00:00:16,354
A palm tree, fully formed.

8
00:00:16,394 --> 00:00:19,279
Between these two pictures: three years.

9
00:00:19,319 --> 00:00:21,637
More than two decades
after that first image,

10
00:00:21,677 --> 00:00:25,967
an astronaut aboard the International
Space Station photographs this coast.

11
00:00:26,007 --> 00:00:28,777
The palm-shaped islands
stand out from orbit.

12
00:00:28,817 --> 00:00:31,482
So how do you build land
where there was only sea?

13
00:00:31,522 --> 00:00:34,187
And what happened
to the plans that came next?

14
00:00:34,227 --> 00:00:39,337
This is Dubai, in the United Arab Emirates,
on the shore of the Persian Gulf.

15
00:00:39,498 --> 00:00:44,248
A coastline seems like the one thing
on a map that nobody gets to choose.

16
00:00:44,409 --> 00:00:46,656
Dubai put that idea to the test.

17
00:00:46,696 --> 00:00:50,540
To see how, we go back to the year 2000.

